      "description": "Watch Club Brugge vs Kortrijk highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League action on August 10, 2026, featured a compelling clash between Club Brugge and KV Kortrijk . Both teams approached the fixture with high energy, looking to secure vital points in a match that promised to be a tactical battle from the very first whistle. Vetlesen Breaks the Deadlock Club Brugge started the contest with clear attacking intent, controlling the tempo and forcing the visitors onto the back foot. Their persistence paid off in the 30th minute when Hugo Vetlesen found the back of the net with a clinical finish. As the first half drew to a close, the tension on the pitch increased, leading to a yellow card for KV Kortrijk defender James Ndjeungoue in the 44th minute after a mistimed challenge. Second Half Surge and Penalty Success The second half began with Club Brugge looking to extend their lead. Despite a caution for Freddie Potts in the 59th minute, the home side remained relentless. In the 69th minute, Mamadou Diakhon turned provider, delivering a precise assist for Carlos Forbs to slot home. The momentum stayed firmly with the hosts, and just five minutes later, Nicolo Tresoldi stepped up to the penalty spot. He made no mistake, firing the ball home in the 74th minute to further consolidate the lead. Tactical Adjustments and Final Whistle As the game entered its final stages, both managers utilized their benches extensively. Club Brugge introduced a wave of fresh legs, including Romeo Vermant and Tian Nai Koren , while KV Kortrijk brought on Felix Lemarechal and Sixtus Ogbuehi in an attempt to find a late response. However, the home side managed the remaining time professionally, ensuring a clean sheet and a comprehensive performance when the referee finally blew the whistle after six minutes of stoppage time."
