      "description": "Watch Club Brugge vs Union St. Gilloise highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 1, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes encounter in the Jupiler Pro League as two of Belgium's most ambitious sides faced off. On August 1, 2026 , fans were treated to a match defined by tactical discipline, sudden shifts in momentum, and an eventual climax that required the ultimate test of nerves. A Tense Opening Half Both Club Brugge and Union St. Gilloise began the contest with a cautious approach, focusing on maintaining their defensive shapes. The game was a physical battle in the middle of the park, with clear-cut chances proving hard to come by. The referee was forced to reach for his pocket in the 39th minute, issuing a yellow card to Carlos Forbs as the intensity of the challenge began to rise. Despite the pressure, neither side could break the deadlock before the interval, leaving the tactical puzzle unsolved at half-time. Goals and Momentum Swings The second half ignited almost immediately. In the 49th minute, Nicolo Tresoldi broke the silence, finishing clinically to put his side ahead. The forward's evening remained eventful as he picked up a booking just minutes later. Union St. Gilloise refused to fade away, searching for a route back into the game. Their persistence paid off in the 77th minute when Kevin Mac Allister found the target, courtesy of an assist from Mohammed Fuseini . Mac Allister had earlier been cautioned, but his crucial strike ensured the match would head toward a dramatic conclusion. Shootout Drama Decides the Day With the scores level at the end of play, the match moved to a penalty shootout. It was a showcase of clinical finishing from the spot, though the tension peaked when Cheveyo Tsawa missed his attempt. For the most part, the shooters were flawless; Relebohile Mofokeng , Romeo Vermant , Adem Zorgane , Besfort Zeneli , Brandon Mechele , Anan Khalaili , Felix Lemarechal , and Promise David all converted with composure. The final word belonged to Nicolo Tresoldi , who stepped up to score the decisive penalty and bring an end to a grueling contest."
